        <p class="profile-detail-region">Battle · Europe</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Verdun</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">21 February to 18 December 1916 (302 days), in four phases</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">The hills on the right (east) bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meuse">Meuse</a> north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/verdun">Verdun</a>, later also the west bank, in the Fortified Region of Verdun, north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>: the 5th Army under Crown Prince Wilhelm, within the plan of Erich von Falkenhayn, with 1,201 guns massed on the front, two thirds heavy or super-heavy. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>: the Second Army and the Fortified Region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/verdun">Verdun</a>, under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippe-petain">Philippe Pétain</a> from late February, then Robert Nivelle, with 388 field guns and 244 heavy guns at the start of the attack</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Germans captured Fort Douaumont and Fort Vaux but never reached the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meuse">Meuse</a> Heights as a secure position; French counter-offensives in October and December recovered both forts and much of the ground. Casualties are put at about 714,000 in all, by Heer and Naumann and by Philpott.</span></div>
        </div>
